Introduction {#intro}
=====================

*This section is non-normative.*

Viewport Capture [[mediacapture-viewport]] and Element Capture [[element-capture]] allow web applications to capture live video streams of the current tab or a specific DOM subtree. However, captured video frames always represent an unclipped rectangular surface, omitting physical screen corner radii, display cutouts, foldable hinges, and form-factor framing.

This specification extends {{CaptureController}} with {{CaptureController/setDeviceFrame()}} so applications and browser automation protocols [[webdriver-bidi]] can composite physical screen masks and vendor-neutral form-factor frames directly in the user agent's capture pipeline.

WebIDL Extensions to CaptureController {#capture-controller-extensions}
=======================================================================

<pre class="idl">
enum CaptureFramingMode {
  "none",
  "occlusions",
  "device"
};

enum DeviceFormFactor {
  "phone",
  "foldable",
  "feature-phone",
  "tablet",
  "notebook",
  "smart-display",
  "watch",
  "desktop"
};

enum DisplayCutoutShape {
  "pill",
  "circle",
  "notch",
  "rectangle"
};

enum CaptureRotationBehavior {
  "resize",
  "contain"
};

dictionary DisplayCutoutInit {
  required DisplayCutoutShape shape;
  required unsigned long x;
  required unsigned long y;
  required unsigned long width;
  required unsigned long height;
  unsigned long borderRadius = 0;
};

dictionary DisplayHingeInit {
  required DOMString orientation;
  required unsigned long offset;
  required unsigned long maskLength;
};

dictionary DeviceFrameConfiguration {
  CaptureFramingMode mode = "device";
  DeviceFormFactor formFactor = "phone";
  (unsigned long or sequence<unsigned long>) cornerRadius = 0;
  sequence<DisplayCutoutInit> cutouts = [];
  DisplayHingeInit? hinge = null;
  CaptureRotationBehavior rotationBehavior = "contain";
  DOMString stageBackground = "#f1f3f4";
};

partial interface CaptureController {
  Promise<undefined> setDeviceFrame(optional DeviceFrameConfiguration? configuration = null);
};
</pre>

## Processing Model for `setDeviceFrame()` ## {#set-device-frame-algorithm}

<div algorithm>
When {{CaptureController/setDeviceFrame(configuration)}} is invoked on a {{CaptureController}} |controller|, the user agent MUST run the following steps:

1. Let |p| be [=a new promise=].
1. If |controller| is not bound to an active display or viewport capture session, [=reject=] |p| with an "{{InvalidStateError}}" {{DOMException}} and return |p|.
1. If |configuration| is `null` or |configuration|["`mode`"] is `"none"`:
   1. Clear any active device-frame stage lock and occlusion mask on |controller|'s capture pipeline.
   1. [=Resolve=] |p| with `undefined` and return |p|.
1. Validate |configuration|:
   1. If |configuration|["`cornerRadius`"] is a sequence whose length is not `4`, [=reject=] |p| with a {{TypeError}} and return |p|.
   1. If |configuration|["`hinge`"] is non-null and |configuration|["`hinge`"]["`orientation`"] is neither `"vertical"` nor `"horizontal"`, [=reject=] |p| with a {{TypeError}} and return |p|.
1. Queue a task on the capture pipeline to apply |configuration| to all subsequent video frames emitted by |controller|'s video track:
   1. Clip the captured surface to |configuration|["`cornerRadius`"].
   1. Composite each cutout in |configuration|["`cutouts`"] and any non-null |configuration|["`hinge`"] over the clipped surface.
   1. If |configuration|["`mode`"] is `"device"`:
      1. Composite a vendor-neutral chassis corresponding to |configuration|["`formFactor`"] over a stage filled with |configuration|["`stageBackground`"].
      1. Round output frame width and height up to even integers (`2n`).
      1. If |configuration|["`rotationBehavior`"] is `"contain"`, lock the output canvas `(width, height)` on first activation and scale subsequent aspect-ratio changes to fit cleanly inside the locked stage.
1. [=Resolve=] |p| with `undefined`.
1. Return |p|.
</div>

WebDriver BiDi Integration Hooks {#webdriver-bidi-hooks}
========================================================

For [[webdriver-bidi]], user agents implementing `emulation.setDisplayFeaturesOverride` and the `framing` parameter (`"none"` | `"occlusions"` | `"device"`) on `browsingContext.captureScreenshot` and `browsingContext.startScreencast` MUST apply the same occlusion-masking and `2n` stage-framing rules defined in [[#set-device-frame-algorithm]] using the active browsing context's emulated display features.

Security and Privacy Considerations {#security-privacy}
=======================================================

* `setDeviceFrame()` consumes synthetic geometry supplied by the caller and MUST NOT expose physical host display cutouts, corner radii, or OEM hardware identifiers.
* `setDeviceFrame()` operates strictly post-capture on frames already authorized by the user's `getViewportMedia()` or `getDisplayMedia()` grant and after any `CropTarget` or `RestrictionTarget` isolation masks have been applied.
